<title>GREECE: RERANKINGS IN GREEK BROKER JANUARY MARKET SHARES.</title>
<headline>RERANKINGS IN GREEK BROKER JANUARY MARKET SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>January trading volume at the</p>
<p>Athens bourse reached 520.7 billion drachmas, a bit below the</p>
<p>577.16 billion traded in December 1996, the Athens stock</p>
<p>exchange members association (SMEHA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The monthly market share rankings showed Sigma Securities</p>
<p>regaining the lead from National Securities with 9.38 percent,</p>
<p>followed by Alpha Credit Bank subsidiary Alpha</p>
<p>Brokerage with 7.59 percent.</p>
<p>National Securities fell to third place with 6.51 percent.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-to-December 1996 trading volume reached</p>
<p>3.979 trillion drachmas. December was last year's best month.</p>
<p>SMEHA released the following data and market share rankings</p>
<p>for December. The top 15 brokers shared 62.5 percent of the</p>
<p>bourse's trading volume. The remainder went to the exchange's</p>
<p>other 47 member brokers.</p>
<p>	BROKER    VOLUME JANUARY	   MARKET SHARE</p>
<p>		    (in drs billion)</p>
<p>1.  Sigma	    49.59			9.38%</p>
<p>2.  Alpha	    40.12			7.59%</p>
<p>3.  National	 34.42			6.51%</p>
<p>4.  Telesis	  30.45			5.76%</p>
<p>5.  Devletoglou    29.05			5.50%</p>
<p>6.  Omega	    19.10			3.61%</p>
<p>7.  Nuntius	  17.24			3.26%</p>
<p>8.  Midland	  16.93			3.20%</p>
<p>9.  Aspis	    15.73			2.98%</p>
<p>10. Ergo	     15.71			2.97%</p>
<p>11. Intersec	 14.17			2.68%</p>
<p>12. Kappa	    12.73			2.41%</p>
<p>13. Commercial     12.29			2.33%</p>
<p>14. Hellenic	 12.28			2.32%</p>
<p>15. ABN AMRO Axias 10.94			2.07%</p>
<p>Total Volume  520.70</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
